  "term": "hereditary ataxia",
  "definition": "Hereditary ataxia is a genetically inherited neurodegenerative disorder marked by ataxia, meaning impaired coordination. It is a heterogeneous condition, with different single-gene causes and varying clinical presentations and age of onset.",
